    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That makes sense. I'm mostly worried about the documentation part. What kind of specific details should I be recording during that first verbal warning to make sure it actually counts if I have to move to a written warning later? I don't want it to seem like I'm just picking on someone.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "For your documentations during the verbal warning, itemize the this poor performance or breach of policy and be as specific as possible. You should note the date and time of the conversation, the employee’s name, what was said, and any suggestions you provided for improvement. It’s also important to express that this is a verbal warning and they will be given the opportunity to correct their behavior before further action is taken. Remember to keep these records in your employee file and always forward any written documentation to the employee, confirming the summary you’ve documented. This helps to showcase your attempts to work with the employee and your adherence to progressive discipline.",
